{"name":"Watercolour Seascape","hex":"#91b4b3","fetched":"2026-10-18","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"watercolour","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A water-soluble pigment or paint.","A painting made by using such pigment."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to the methods or products of watercolor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/watercolour"},{"term":"seascape","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A view of the sea.","A piece of art that depicts the sea or shoreline."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seascape"}],"entries":[{"title":"Watercolor painting","blocks":[{"text":"Watercolor or watercolour, also aquarelle, is a painting method in which the paints are made of pigments suspended in a water-based solution. Watercolor refers to both the medium and the resulting artwork."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Dolceacqua43_-_Artista_locale_mentre_dipinge_un_acquarello.jpg/330px-Dolceacqua43_-_Artista_locale_mentre_dipinge_un_acquarello.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watercolor_painting","wikidata":"Q50030"},{"title":"Seascape","blocks":[{"text":"A seascape is a photograph, painting, or other work of art which depicts the sea, in other words an example of marine art. The word originated as a formation from landscape, which was first used for images of land in art. By a similar development, \"seascape\" has also come to mean actual perceptions of the sea itself. It is applied in planning contexts to geographical locations possessing a good view of the sea. Seascape aesthetics receive legal protection in terms of biodiversity/ health of the seas (the OSPAR Convention, and in terms of the visual bio-cultural seascape."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/The_Wave_-_Pierre-Auguste_Renoir_-_Google_Cultural_Institute.jpg/330px-The_Wave_-_Pierre-Auguste_Renoi